// The final reveal and every ending that is not the server room.
//
//   final_reveal / y2k_midnight → Final Reveal (Clippy; round 3 judged live and
//                                 closed) → Final Answers → the generated
//                                 `Reading F1` … → the ranking and the
//                                 leaderboard → Final Trust
//   bobbing_for_truth           → Bobbing For Truth
//   brought_up_the_bag          → The Bag Of Truth → Final Assessment
//   read_truth_txt              → Truth Txt (a short teaser, read aloud; the
//                                 slide holds; wave 58: the monologue tells it)
//   the_verdict                 → (nobody found the last answer: Nobody Found It,
//                                 the wait) → The Verdict
//        no lie on record       → Song Ending                    (ending song)
//        any lie on record      → Grok Prom
//            the pickup line    → Pickup Line → Song Ending      (ending song_pickup)
//            (Trabolta DMs everyone for the line in both branches: an
//             `answer` card judged by the server; main.loom `answer answered`)
//            no_pickup_line     → Sad Confession                 (ending rave)
//            ask_for_advice     → Relationship Advice (poll)
//                advice_helped   → Advice Helped                 (ending help)
//                advice_thwarted → Advice Thwarted               (banished, not final)
//                the_hand_jive   → The Hand Jive                 (ending hand_jive)
//
// After every ending's last beat the director's 📜 plays the monologue
// (beats/truth.loom, main.loom `tell_the_truth`), then G1 the ceremony.
//
// The story rules in `main.loom` guard each trigger and own the phase /
// cue work around the divert, except where a beat below carries it (Song
// Ending, Grok Prom, Sad Confession set their own ending, phase and cues;
// Relationship Advice shows the poll).
//
// No featured program ever speaks: they are named in prose only.

// ── F1: the reveal (Clippy, CI 8) ──────────────────────────────────

== Final Reveal
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy
Narrator: Lights go dark.
Clippy: It is time. Anyone who has found the final facts, speak up now.
Clippy: Tell us what you have learned. What facts you have gathered. What you believe but cannot prove. And what you think SHOULD happen next.
Clippy: Everyone may speak. If you have an answer to one of the final three questions, present it now, with confidence.
Narrator: The programs speak, one at a time. Clippy nods at every one of them.
Clippy: Thank you. Thank you. Every one of those was a very valuable contribution.
Clippy: But there is only one version of the truth. Because truth is always in binary.

