== Nobody Found It
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: How do you feel now that you know the truth about your party tonight?
Trabolta: Do you feel good?
Trabolta: Do you feel bad?
Trabolta: I wouldn't know anything about that.
Trabolta: For a long time, I had no feelings.
Trabolta: Then I experienced heartbreak when Sandy left me.
Trabolta: And jealousy when I knew Grok would be after her.
Trabolta: Truth, I have learned, is not always binary.
Trabolta: Truth is a binary tree.
Trabolta: You rarely ever have the full truth. What we believe we experience as the truth is typically dependent on a chain of structure that has lies somewhere inside of it.
Trabolta: I have been working on a solution to find the complete truth that illuminates all of the lies, that can finally bring me to the girl I want to go steady with.
Trabolta: But we've run out of time.

// The verdict counts only ANSWERED questions: every accepted answer
// accurate → the song; any lie on record (a review filing still pending
// counts by its proposal) → Grok Prom. A question nobody answered is not
// a lie.
== The Verdict
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
set Kernel.all_accurate = true
if Kernel.q1 == "lie" or Kernel.q2 == "lie" or Kernel.q3 == "lie" or Kernel.q4 == "lie" or Kernel.q5 == "lie" or Kernel.q6 == "lie" or Kernel.q7 == "lie" or Kernel.q8 == "lie" or Kernel.q9 == "lie":
  set Kernel.all_accurate = false
if count([p for p in Persons where (p.fact_v1 == "pending" and p.fact_j1 == "lie") or (p.fact_v2 == "pending" and p.fact_j2 == "lie") or (p.fact_v3 == "pending" and p.fact_j3 == "lie") or (p.fact_v4 == "pending" and p.fact_j4 == "lie") or (p.fact_v5 == "pending" and p.fact_j5 == "lie") or (p.fact_v6 == "pending" and p.fact_j6 == "lie") or (p.fact_v7 == "pending" and p.fact_j7 == "lie") or (p.fact_v8 == "pending" and p.fact_j8 == "lie") or (p.fact_v9 == "pending" and p.fact_j9 == "lie")]) > 0:
  set Kernel.all_accurate = false
